-- =============================================================
-- Costmatic — catalog seed: Pakistani kirana (984 products)
--
-- Generated from Pakistan_Kirana_Products_LocalShop_Filtered.xlsx (38 category
-- sheets). NOT a migration — catalog data must not run against staging or the
-- second client's project. Apply by hand, once:
--
--   psql "$DATABASE_URL" -f supabase/seeds/catalog_kirana_pakistan.sql
--
-- Re-runnable: a product already in the catalog is skipped, never duplicated.
--
-- ── Everything lands INACTIVE ───────────────────────────────
-- This is the market, not one shop's shelf. Every row is is_active = false
-- with no prices, so none of it can reach the POS. The owner prices what they
-- actually stock and ticks it active.
--
-- ── Units, retail AND wholesale ─────────────────────────────
-- Base unit is the single piece (or the kilo for pansaari loose goods, which
-- sell fractionally). Where the sheet gave a real pack count, the bulk unit —
-- carton, box, bag, crate, bora, tray, jar — is added with that factor. Both
-- units are sellable retail and wholesale, matching how a kirana counter works.
--
-- Where the sheet only said "approx — confirm with distributor" no bulk unit is
-- invented; the product gets its base unit and the owner adds the carton with
-- the real count from the Packs & Prices step.
--
-- Prices are deliberately absent — Pakistani rates move weekly.
-- =============================================================

